# After five heads in a row, is tails more likely?
subtitle: "Five heads in a row: is tails now due? Guess, then hear why the coin has no memory, and how a Monte Carlo roulette wheel cost gamblers millions."

## After five heads in a row, is tails more likely?
sources:
    - id: mc
      title: Gambler's fallacy
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gambler's_fallacy
      finding: at the Monte Carlo Casino on 18 August 1913, black came up 26 times in a row; gamblers lost millions betting on red

    circle h1 "H" #2f6b8f x 120 y 410 width 136 font_size 56 hidden true
    circle h2 "H" #2f6b8f x 272 y 410 width 136 font_size 56 hidden true
    circle h3 "H" #2f6b8f x 424 y 410 width 136 font_size 56 hidden true
    circle h4 "H" #2f6b8f x 576 y 410 width 136 font_size 56 hidden true
    circle h5 "H" #2f6b8f x 728 y 410 width 136 font_size 56 hidden true
    circle next "?" #b5482e x 880 y 410 width 136 font_size 56 hidden true
    group heads members ["h1","h2","h3","h4","h5"] hidden true
    text fifty "50 : 50" #b5482e x 880 y 255 font_size 56 hidden true
    text odds "1 in 32" #2f6b8f x 424 y 255 font_size 56 hidden true
    text big "26" #222222 cites ["mc"] x 500 y 470 font_size 200 hidden true
    text bets "bets on red" #b5482e x 800 y 470 font_size 48 hidden true
    text big_l "blacks in a row" x 500 y 320 font_size 52 hidden true

    card title "Five heads in a row: what next?"

A: You toss a fair coin five times, and it lands heads every time. What comes next?
    draw heads

B: Tails, obviously. It's overdue!
    draw next

    quiz "After five heads in a row, what is the chance the next toss is tails?"
        right: Exactly half. The coin has no memory: every toss starts from scratch.
        wrong: Ask what the coin remembers.
        * More than half
        + Exactly half
        * Less than half

B: But five heads in a row is rare. Doesn't that count for something?
    draw fifty

A: It is rare: one chance in thirty-two.
    draw odds

A: But those five are already done. Only the next toss is still open, and it is a plain coin toss.
    highlight next

    erase heads next fifty odds

B: Tell that to a casino.
    text where "Monte Carlo, 1913" #8f887c x 500 y 610 font_size 44

A: Funny you should say that. In Monte (@draw big big_l@) Carlo, in August 1913, a roulette ball landed on black twenty-six times in a row.

A: Gamblers piled their money on red, sure it was due. They lost millions.
    draw bets

B: So the gambler's fallacy has a home address.
    text fall "the Monte Carlo fallacy" #b5482e x 500 y 215 font_size 44

A: It does. It's often called the Monte Carlo fallacy, and the wheel never knew it was on a streak.
    highlight fall
